        "zh-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "309f1502-5a5b-3082-ae0b-4b2d81dc3b60",
                "word": "puerile",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5a823444-9094-47b8-bab1-d2739cf6ccca",
                        "entry_id": "309f1502-5a5b-3082-ae0b-4b2d81dc3b60",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more puerile"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "7424ea52-bd62-4b69-aa77-71314de08554",
                        "entry_id": "309f1502-5a5b-3082-ae0b-4b2d81dc3b60",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most puerile"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "85d583c9-0a3e-3901-a3e7-06fb088436c2",
                        "entry_id": "309f1502-5a5b-3082-ae0b-4b2d81dc3b60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "幼稚的，天真的；愚蠢的"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0b70cae-2923-48e3-a639-4d55a97c2aed",
                                "sense_id": "85d583c9-0a3e-3901-a3e7-06fb088436c2",
                                "text": "The French have been notorious through generations for their puerile affectation of Roman forms, models, and historic precedents."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7e64cb0-e2f9-4373-8d70-84ff5158ff11",
                                "sense_id": "85d583c9-0a3e-3901-a3e7-06fb088436c2",
                                "text": "源自the table he had received the gout; from the alcove a tendency to convulsions; from the grandeeship a pride so vast and puerile that he seldom heard anything that was said to him and talked to the ceiling in a perpetual monologue; from the exile, oceans of boredom, a boredom so persuasive that it was like pain,—he woke up with it and spent the day with it, and it sat by his bed all night watching his sleep."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2499c13-78a0-480a-8eaa-c939c2123afc",
                                "sense_id": "85d583c9-0a3e-3901-a3e7-06fb088436c2",
                                "text": "[…] I have always found it hard that Hamlet, a character that I love and admire, is guilty of a puerile misogyny and, perhaps, more worryingly, of the unnecessary deaths of his old friends from university, Rosencrantz and Guildenstern。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e9bf502-e578-4d26-a0ae-482d45a5281d",
                                "sense_id": "85d583c9-0a3e-3901-a3e7-06fb088436c2",
                                "text": "Today we should welcome, and even study, every serious attempt to envisage the future of our race, not merely to grasp the very diverse and often tragic possibilities that confront us, but also that we may familiarize ourselves with the certainty that many of our cherished ideals would seem puerile to more developed minds."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b15dfea5-2eaa-3ab1-84d1-1f0905be032f",
                        "entry_id": "309f1502-5a5b-3082-ae0b-4b2d81dc3b60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "男孩的"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
